1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,121
Ed White walked in space in 1965. Then he died in a fire.

2
00:00:04,233 --> 00:00:07,990
June 3, 1965. Gemini 4 is orbiting Earth.

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,799
Ed White becomes the first American to walk in space.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,674
A golden tether links him to the capsule.

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,355
He moves with a handheld gun that fires bursts of oxygen.

6
00:00:15,467 --> 00:00:17,253
Each burst pushes him a little farther away.

7
00:00:17,367 --> 00:00:20,136
Earth rolls beneath him, more than a hundred miles down.

8
00:00:20,267 --> 00:00:23,423
After about twenty-one minutes, mission control calls him back.

9
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:25,779
He does not want to come back in. But he does.

10
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,111
Four days after launch, the crew splashes down safely.

11
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:34,973
January 27, 1967. White is preparing for a launch rehearsal on Apollo 1.

12
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,087
A fire breaks out inside the capsule.

13
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,936
White dies, with Gus Grissom and Roger Chaffee.

14
00:00:40,067 --> 00:00:42,590
His only spacewalk was the one that made him famous.
